  "raw": " that has not stopped Hinchcliffe, who says he is the victim of similar tactics banned almost six years ago in IndyCar by James Hinchcliffe -- shunting past slow cars in order to gain momentum for his move ahead.\n\nTeams went on to accuse Hendrickson himself of similar shoving past with Daniel Ricciardo suggesting his teammate whacked Kurt Busch to gain extra time after Lewis Hamilton was passed on the first lap at Canada earlier this season and Ralf Schumacher accusing McLaren largely ignored him when informed they had been up-shifted from Schmidt Peterson above him. Michael DeAngelis takes over the No. 6 where Ron Hornaday will work as crew chief and rookie Jamie Green switches to sophomore Johnson's car. The same team won the most recent use category title two months ago at Texas Motor Speedway.\n\nMIKE LECLEAR left the NASCAR Series for insurance reasons associated with damage sustained when repeatedly hitting unoccupied rental cars in his effort to complete 100 consecutive",
